  "notes": "Source: official 2024-2025 Bastyr University catalog, BS in Herbal Sciences (quarter system; 6 quarters sequenced exactly as the catalog's quarterly tables print them). The catalog's published graduation total is 90 credits = 84 core + 6 elective; this seed sequences the 84 core credits and the 6 elective credits are not assigned to any quarter in the catalog, so total_credits is the sum of sequenced course credits only. The catalog requires that four of the elective credits be in Botanical Medicine field classes. Catalog scheduling note: BO4802 Herbal Sciences Practicum may be taken any quarter after winter of the junior year (sequenced as printed). Upper-division completion program: admission requires 90 quarter credits from a regionally accredited institution; the bachelor's requires 180 credits total inclusive of transfer, with a minimum 2.0 GPA and 45 quarter credits in residence at Bastyr. [Coordinator 2026-10-01: genuine 6-quarter BS (Bastyr quarter system); pipeline-excluded by build.py's bachelor 8-12 semester gate (quarter-system precedent).]",
